THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

The full, generated dependency inventory lives in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md and is
refreshed in CI (cargo-about for the Rust tree, license-checker for the npm
tree). It is also shown in-app under Settings -> Advanced, as GPL-3 requires.
The summary below covers the primary components and is not a substitute for that
file.

  gitoxide (gix)          MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Tauri 2                 MIT OR Apache-2.0
  serde, serde_json       MIT OR Apache-2.0
  notify                  CC0-1.0 OR Artistic-2.0
  Svelte / SvelteKit      MIT
  Vite                    MIT

All are compatible with distribution inside a GPL-3.0-or-later work.


FONTS
-----

GitLumiere ships no bundled font. The UI uses the host platform's system font
stack. The design handoff wireframes used "Architects Daughter" to signal draft
status; it is deliberately not shipped.

If a font is bundled in future, its license (OFL or otherwise) must be stated
here and its text included in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md.


ICONS
-----

Glyphs in the UI are Unicode text characters, which carry no license. Any icon
set added later must be MIT/OFL or an original commissioned mark, relicensable
under GPL-3.0-or-later, and must be recorded here.


CORRESPONDING SOURCE
--------------------

The commit SHA of each build is embedded at compile time and displayed in
Settings -> Advanced -> About, alongside a link to the corresponding source for
that exact build.
